{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>ילפתו</b> — They twist, as in \"and the man trembled and ילפת,\" and \"Shimshon וילפת.\" The meaning concerns the streams, that they rise as vapor, and the matter is that the nature of waters is to descend downward, and when they turn to vapor, they go up into nothingness and perish. And the commentators interpret this verse as referring to those who travel desert routes, and it is not correct."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:59.309780363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}